# .planning/ is GSD's machine-written, machine-read working area. Prettier's
# markdown formatting corrupts it in at least three distinct ways, each verified
# on this repo:
#
#   1. Table padding breaks the broken-windows ledger. gsd-tools locates the
#      rendered table in WINDOWS.md by scanning for an UNPADDED literal header
#      line (TABLE_HEADER_LINE in gsd-core/bin/lib/broken-windows.cjs). Prettier
#      pads table columns to align them, the scan then fails, and every
#      `gsd-tools windows append/waive/fixed` write is refused with "Ledger
#      table region could not be located" — leaving the ledger read-only.
#
#   2. proseWrap: always rewraps executable content in PLAN.md files. Shell
#      commands inside <automated> gates get split across lines into unrunnable
#      fragments, and consecutive lines inside blocks like <execution_context>
#      are collapsed onto one line.
#
#   3. Emphasis normalisation rewrites regexes. Two `*` characters on adjacent
#      lines are paired as markdown emphasis and the delimiter is normalised to
#      `_`, silently turning `grep -v '^[[:space:]]*#'` into
#      `grep -v '^[[:space:]]_#'` — a disabled filter that still looks correct.
#
# Case 3 is the dangerous one: it leaves a gate that passes for the wrong
# reason. Formatting buys nothing here (nobody reads these as prose), so the
# whole directory is excluded rather than patched file by file.
#
# The ledger's table must not be hand-edited either way; the fenced JSON block
# below it is the sole source of truth.
.planning/
